SwiftPutty local patch 0012
Upstream: PuTTY 0.85 (a3cce3a48d4ab12e0fccb32998b9042d4f7c3ff1)
Status:   not yet reported upstream; suitable for upstream

Telnet and local proxies: format the proxy command a second time only
after prompting.

Both negotiators format the command, and when it needs a user name or
password they don't have, discard it, prompt, and format it again with
the answers. The second format was outside the prompting branch, so it
also ran when no prompt was needed and overwrote (leaked) the first
result, which still held the proxy password when one was configured.
Found by `leaks --atExit` on Core/tests/spb_backends_test.c. The second
format now happens only after the prompts, as its comment says.

--- a/proxy/telnet.c
+++ b/proxy/telnet.c
@@ -148,14 +148,14 @@
 
             free_prompts(s->prompts);
             s->prompts = NULL;
-        }
 
-        /*
-         * Now format the command a second time, with the results of
-         * those prompts written into s->conf.
-         */
-        s->formatted_cmd = format_telnet_command(
-            pn->ps->remote_addr, pn->ps->remote_port, s->conf, NULL);
+            /*
+             * Now format the command a second time, with the results of
+             * those prompts written into s->conf.
+             */
+            s->formatted_cmd = format_telnet_command(
+                pn->ps->remote_addr, pn->ps->remote_port, s->conf, NULL);
+        }
     }
 
     /*
